      "writtenOn": "2023-04-05T07:02:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After aosp/2519918, would it be possible to update mTetherInterfaceSockets to be a  ArrayMap\u003cNetworkKey, SocketInfo\u003e, where you\u0027d have different NetworkKey instances that contain the interface index ?\n\nThis way the interface index is already \"cached\" in the NetworkKey, so no need to maintain a mIfaceNameToIndexMap.\n\nI think it would remove the need for getAndUpdateInterfaceIndex, if you just call getNetworkInterfaceIndexByName in handleTetherInterfacesChanged or requestSocket (so just once before creating each socket). Also mTetherInterfaceSockets and mNetworkSockets could be merged to simplify logic.\n\nI\u0027m concerned about races when updating mIfaceNameToIndexMap, so I\u0027d rather have most of the code use interface indexes instead of converting from the name.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 346,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 346,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "6ee4442e9891201186514a0912b325656c7d12bf",
